<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head with-photo">
    <div>
      <h1>Trades for mine sites, camps and workshops</h1>
      <p>For the smaller jobs that don't need a full tender. That covers camp and village maintenance, workshop repairs, fabrication, and work on site offices. Post the job with the site requirements and get quotes from tradies who already hold the tickets.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn accent big" href="/jobs/new?sector=mining">Post a mining job</a></p>
    </div>
    <%- include('../partials/photo', { photo: 'goldfieldsMine', eager: true }) %>
  </div>

  <div class="split page" style="padding-top:8px">
    <div class="doc">
      <h2>What gets posted</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list">
        <li>Camp room repairs and air con</li>
        <li>Plumbing in ablution blocks and kitchens</li>
        <li>Electrical work in site offices and dongas</li>
        <li>Welding repairs and fabrication</li>
        <li>Mechanical fitting in workshops</li>
        <li>Scaffolding</li>
        <li>Concrete pads, footings and paths</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="doc">
      <h2>Site requirements up front</h2>
      <p>Every mining job has to list what's needed to get on site: inductions, tickets, medicals, PPE, and whether it's FIFO or DIDO with flights, meals and accommodation covered. Tradies quote knowing all of that.</p>
      <p>Tradies list their tickets and inductions on their profile, so you can check them before you accept a quote.</p>
      <h2>Contractor approval</h2>
      <p>If your site only lets approved contractors on, check that the tradie is on your vendor list, or can be added, before you accept. We check ABN and insurance, but that doesn't replace your site's own approval process.</p>
      <h2>Where</h2>
      <p>Pilbara, Goldfields, Mid West, Kimberley and anywhere else in WA. Tradies choose the regions they'll travel to.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/sector-jobs') %>
